{
  "requirement": "Give `search_structure` the language and an ast-grep rule. Use `prefix` to\nnarrow the search and `limit` to cap matches. Each match carries a source\naddress for `read_source` and a tag for `finish_search`.\nFor the `instructions` field, see {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.search.first_search.instructions`.\n\n```text\nsearch_structure({language: string, rule: object, prefix?: string, limit?: integer})\n  -> {search_id: UUID, instructions?: string, next?: UUID, complete: boolean, matches: {tag: string, node: {path: string, selector: string}, excerpt: string}[]}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural obligations in `requirements.sdk.graph.search.search_structure.mcp` are met.\n\n**Input schema.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#impl[Session<'_, D>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` declares `search_structure` with `language` (string) and `rule` (object) as required. It declares `prefix` (string) and `limit` (integer, minimum 0) as optional properties.\n\n**Dispatch.** In `fn[dispatch]` of the same impl, the `search_structure` arm reads `language` as a string and `rule` as an object. It reads `prefix` into the scope and `limit` as an optional nonnegative integer. These go into a `StructuralQuery`, which has `scope`, `language`, `rule` and `limit`.\n\n**Output shape.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/pages.rs#impl[Pages<N, L>]/fn[search]` builds each page. A page has `search_id` (a UUID), `complete`, and `matches`.\n- Each match entry gets a `tag` string.\n- The `search_structure` arm builds each entry as `{node, excerpt}`. `node` is an `OutlineId` that serializes as `{path, selector}`, and `excerpt` is the redacted excerpt.\n- `instructions` is set only on the first page of the first search. This is the field the cited `first_search.instructions` requirement describes.\n- `next` is set to the UUID of the following page.\n\n**Coverage of the signature.** The schema, the dispatch and the page builder together cover every field in the required signature. Each tag is also recorded in the page's `SearchPage` entries, which is how a later `finish_search` call resolves it.\n\n**Out of scope.** The `instructions` content belongs to the cited requirement, so I did not assess it here.\n\nNo gaps were found, and there are no acknowledgments.",
  "references": "204dce9f4641383b47bc8843fef8eb7b13f4765bbd0037ce9278d1b81f8ce49b",
